    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0426" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War/9–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador to the Greek
                        Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Cairo</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-12T20:00:00-04:00">September 12,
                            1944—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Reurtel 305, September 12. Department has no objection to Moshanov’s
                    departure for Ankara.</p>
                <p>For your information the Soviet Government has proposed that the Bulgarian terms
                    be presented either at Moscow or at Ankara. We are indicating a preference for
                    Ankara, but are not yet informed <pb facs="0427" n="415" xml:id="pg415"/> of the
                    British views. We are also agreeing to having the EAC review the terms and
                    examine certain as yet undisclosed “amendments and additions” which the Russians
                    wish to propose.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
